                        <h2>7. FAQs — US Rent Reporting</h2>
                        <h3>Does paying rent build credit in the US?</h3>
                        <p>Only if your landlord or a rent reporting service reports it to Experian, Equifax, or TransUnion. On-time payments can add a tradeline and help thin files +10-20 points. Late payments hurt.</p>
                        <h3>Will rent reporting require my SSN?</h3>
                        <p>Bureaus need SSN or ITIN to match. Boom, Pinata allow ITIN. You can sign up without SSN to test, but for actual reporting you'll provide ID. Services encrypt data per CFPB guidance.</p>
                        <h3>Which credit bureaus count rent?</h3>
                        <p>Experian sees rent via RentBureau. Equifax and TransUnion accept rent tradelines. VantageScore counts rent. FICO 10T counts rent better than FICO 8. Most mortgage lenders use FICO 2/4/5 — VantageScore lift helps for cards, less for mortgage initially.</p>
                        <h3>Can rent reporting hurt my credit?</h3>
                        <p>Yes — if late 30+ days, similar to loan. Collection on unpaid rent hurts severely. Always set autopay.</p>
                        <h3>How long does rent stay on report?</h3>
                        <p>Up to 7 years, like other accounts. Closed positive rent stays up to 10 years per Equifax.</p>
                        <h3>Is Piñata / Boom / RentTrack / Esusu legit?</h3>
                        <p>Yes — all 4 operate nationwide, report to US bureaus, BBB listed. Check reviews before paying. Avoid any that ask to change payee to them — legitimate services verify payments, don't collect rent.</p>

                        <h2>Sources & Compliance</h2>
                        <p class="text-[12px]">Sources: <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/" class="underline">CFPB Ask CFPB - What is a credit report</a>, <a href="https://www.experian.com/blogs/ask-experian/does-paying-rent-build-credit/" class="underline">Experian - Does Paying Rent Build Credit</a>, <a href="https://www.equifax.com/personal/education/credit-score/articles/gl/does-paying-rent-help-credit-scores/" class="underline">Equifax - Does Paying Rent Help Credit</a>, TransUnion SmartMove 2023-2024 Thin File Study. Educational purpose only. Not financial advice. ScoreUp not affiliated with Boom, RentTrack, Pinata, Esusu. Update verification for Oct 20, 2026.</p>
                        <p class="text-[12px]">Methodology note: +12 points headline is based on TransUnion thin-file median lift + hypothetical 24-month back-report example — not a guarantee. Actual lift varies by file, bureaus, scoring model.</p>
